<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōtĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		moveo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a moving, motion; a removing</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">principium motionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fat. 19, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					N. D. 2, 58, 145</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab ordine motio,</span>”
				<i>a removing</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					47, 20, 3</span></i>
			.—Abstr., <i>motion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipsum animum ... quasi quamdam continuatam
					motionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 1, 10, 22</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			partic., in medicine, <i>an ague-fit</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 3, 5,
				28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: motiones animi, <i>emotions</i> or <i>affections of the soul</i>
			(old reading), <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 1, 8</span></i>; better,
			notionibus.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
